1:% 0_facts.pl : the PROPOSED canonical HTTP surface facts.
3:% Lab-local on purpose. On landing these rows move into
4:% v6/prolog/compile/registry.pl beside cli_command/3 and the existing
5:% http_route/3, and this file disappears (lab protocol: labs die on landing).
6:% Nothing in v6/prolog/compile/ or v6/tsv2/ is edited by this lab.
8:% ── why these shapes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
10:% registry.pl already carries http_route(Method, Path, Summary) -- three
11:% columns, enough to generate a CLI inventory and detect route drift, not
12:% enough to generate a spec. What a spec needs on top is exactly: an operation
13:% NAME (stable across renames of the path), the PARAMETERS, the REQUEST body,
14:% and the RESPONSE set. Those become four more tables rather than four more
15:% columns, for the same reason registry.pl keeps surface/5 and expression/5
16:% apart: a route with no body should not carry a body column.
18:%   http_operation(OpId, Method, PathTemplate, Summary)
19:%   http_path_param(OpId, Name, Type, Description)
20:%   http_query_param(OpId, Name, Type, Required, Description)
21:%   http_request_body(OpId, MediaType, TypeExpr, Required, Description)
22:%   http_response(OpId, Status, MediaType, TypeExpr, Description)
24:% PathTemplate keeps the SERVER'S own `:rel` spelling (4_http.ts and the
25:% generated cli/0_inventory.ts both use it). Translating to OpenAPI's `{rel}`
26:% is the emitter's job, so the facts stay target-neutral -- the same rule the
27:% tsv2 plan term follows (target-neutral term, target-specific emission).
29:% ── the type vocabulary ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
31:% TypeExpr reuses the existing column-type words wherever they say the right
32:% thing (0_type_plane.pl: int / text / bool / float / a rel name in column
33:% position) and adds only what a wire boundary needs that a stored column
34:% does not:
36:%   text | int | bool | float        the scalar words, unchanged
37:%   list(TypeExpr)                   JSON array
38:%   schema(Name)                     $ref to a named schema below
39:%   enum([Atom, ...])                closed string set
40:%   one_of([TypeExpr, ...])          union; OpenAPI 3.1 only (see plan doc)
42:% Deliberately ABSENT: null. rulings say null never (Option is variants or
43:% absence), and no route on the current surface returns one.
45:%   http_schema(Name, object, Description)
46:%   http_schema(Name, alias(TypeExpr), Description)
47:%   http_schema_field(Name, Field, TypeExpr, Required, Description)
49:% Field ORDER is source order and is significant in the emitted spec's
50:% property list, matching decl_column_spelling's "source order significant"
51:% ruling for rel columns.
